rds":[{"surface":"வெண்","parts":[{"text":"வெண்","lemma":"வெண்","gloss":"white"}],"gloss":"white","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தலை","parts":[{"text":"தலை","lemma":"talai","gloss":"head"}],"gloss":"headed"},{"surface":"புணரி","parts":[{"text":"புணரி","lemma":"puṇari","gloss":"ocean wave"}],"gloss":"waves"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மான்குளம்பு","parts":[{"text":"மான்","lemma":"māṉ","gloss":"horse/deer"},{"text":"குளம்பு","lemma":"kuḷampu","gloss":"hoof"}],"gloss":"horses' hooves"},{"surface":"அலைப்ப","parts":[{"text":"அலை","lemma":"alai","gloss":"wave/shake"},{"text":"ப்ப","lemma":"ppa","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to splash"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வலமுறை","parts":[{"text":"வலம்","lemma":"valam","gloss":"right side/victory"},{"text":"முறை","lemma":"muṟai","gloss":"manner"}],"gloss":"in a clockwise manner"},{"surface":"வருதலும்","parts":[{"text":"வருதல்","lemma":"varutal","gloss":"coming"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and coming"},{"surface":"உண்டு","parts":[{"text":"உண்டு","lemma":"uṇṭu","gloss":"exists"}],"gloss":"is certain"},{"surface":"என்று","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"say"},{"text":"து","lemma":"tu","gloss":"absolutive suffix"}],"gloss":"having said"},{"surface":"அலமந்து","parts":[{"text":"அலமந்து","lemma":"அலமந்து","gloss":"having been distressed"}],"gloss":"having been distressed","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெஞ்சு","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சு","lemma":"neñcu","gloss":"heart"}],"gloss":"heart"},{"surface":"நடுங்கு","parts":[{"text":"நடுங்கு","lemma":"naṭuṅku","gloss":"tremble"}],"gloss":"trembling"},{"surface":"அவலம்","parts":[{"text":"அவலம்","lemma":"avalam","gloss":"distress"}],"gloss":"sorrow"},{"surface":"பாயத்","parts":[{"text":"பாயத்","lemma":"பாயத்","gloss":"to spread"}],"gloss":"to spread","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"துஞ்சா","parts":[{"text":"துஞ்சு","lemma":"tuñcu","gloss":"sleep"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"negative relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"sleepless"},{"surface":"கண்ண","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"eye"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"possessing suffix"}],"gloss":"possessing eyes"},{"surface":"வட","parts":[{"text":"வட","lemma":"வட","gloss":"northern"}],"gloss":"northern","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புலத்து","parts":[{"text":"புலத்து","lemma":"புலத்து","gloss":"of the land"}],"gloss":"of the land","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அரசே","parts":[{"text":"அரசு","lemma":"aracu","gloss":"king"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"vocative suffix"}],"gloss":"O kings!"}]}],"literal":"Excellent traditional wealth and pleasure / follow righteousness, like that appearance, / two umbrellas falling behind, rising high, one umbrella / like the fear-inspiring moon, rising far away to shine, / seeking the hunt of good fame, in victorious war / battle camp except, you are not indeed! / The source of wealth to diminish, having attacked, enemies' / protected fortress wall leaping upon, your male elephants do not stay quiet. / War if one says, desiring, wearing warrior anklets, brave warriors, / in the forest lying, countries very distant, / 'we will go, we are not' they do not say, with a loud noise / festive in those places in foreign lands having camped, / eastern sea being behind, western sea / white-headed waves your horses' hooves to splash, / clockwise coming is certain, having said, having been distressed, / heart-trembling sorrow to spread, / sleepless possessing eyes, northern land kings!","translation":"Just as wealth and pleasure follow the path of righteousness according to excellent tradition, your single umbrella rises high, making the umbrellas of the other two kings fall behind, and shines far away like the awe-inspiring full moon. Seeking only the pursuit of great fame, you are never found anywhere except in your victorious battle camps! Your war elephants, which charge so fiercely that the wealth of your enemies is ruined, never stay quiet as they batter the guarded fortress walls of your foes. Your brave warriors, adorned with warrior anklets, who rejoice at the very mention of war, never say, 'We will not go,' even when the lands they must cross lie far away beyond dense forests. Camping with a loud roar in those festive foreign lands, your horses splash their hooves in the white-crested waves of the western sea while the eastern sea lies far behind. Realizing that your victorious march around the world is certain, the kings of the north are filled with distress, their hearts trembling with sorrow, and their eyes remain sleepless.","modern":"சிறப்புடைய மரபின்படி பொருளும் இன்பமும் அறத்தின் வழியே செல்லும் தோற்றத்தைப் போல, சேர பாண்டியர்களின் இரு குடைகளும் பின்வாங்க, உனது ஒற்றைக் குடை மட்டும் அச்சம் தரும் முழுமதியைப் போல உயர்ந்து விளங்குகின்றது. நல்ல புகழைப் பெற விரும்பி, நீ எப்போதும் வெற்றி தரும் போர்ப் பாசறையிலேயே தங்கியிருக்கிறாய். பகைவர்களின் செல்வ வளம் அழியுமாறு தாக்கி, அவர்களின் காவல் மிகுந்த மதில்களைப் பாயும் உனது யானைகள் சும்மா இருப்பதில்லை. போர் என்று சொன்னாலே விரும்பும் வீரக்கழல் அணிந்த உனது வீரர்கள், காடுகளுக்கு அப்பால் உள்ள நாடுகள் மிகத் தொலைவில் இருந்தாலும், 'நாங்கள் போகமாட்டோம்' என்று கூறாமல் ஆரவாரத்துடன் புறப்படுகின்றனர். விழாக்கள் நிறைந்த பகைவர்களின் நாடுகளில் தங்கி, கிழக்குக் கடல் பின்னே இருக்க, மேற்குக் கடலின் வெள்ளையலைகளில் உனது குதிரைகளின் குளம்புகள் பாய்கின்றன. நீ உலகை வலம் வந்து வெல்வது உறுதி என்று எண்ணி, வடநாட்டு மன்னர்கள் நெஞ்சு நடுங்கும் துயரத்துடன் தூங்காத கண்களோடு இருக்கிறார்கள்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai (victory) and specifically the Arasavākai theme, which praises the greatness and righteous rule of a king. The poet, Kōvūr Kiḻār, addresses the Chola king Nalaṅkiḷḷi, praising his relentless military campaigns and global ambition. The poet uses a powerful simile in the opening lines, comparing the king's single sovereign umbrella to righteousness (aṟam), while wealth (poruḷ) and pleasure (iṉpam) follow it, just as the other two Tamil kings (Chera and Pandya) are forced to submit to his rule. The imagery of the Chola horses splashing in the western sea while the eastern sea is behind them highlights the vastness of his conquests from coast to coast. The poem concludes by describing the psychological impact of Nalaṅkiḷḷi's unstoppable army on the northern kings, who lie awake in terror, anticipating his victorious march.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.42],[0.42,0.76],[0.76,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,1.97],[1.97,2.8],[2.8,3.3],[3.3,3.7],[3.7,4.17],[4.17,4.85],[4.85,5.4],[5.4,5.8],[5.8,6.0],[6.0,6.2],[6.2,7.1],[7.1,7.4],[7.4,8.2],[8.2,8.6],[8.6,9.14],[9.14,9.68],[9.68,10.08],[10.08,10.4],[10.4,11.21],[11.21,12.3],[12.3,12.91],[12.91,13.2],[13.2,14.4],[14.4,14.9],[14.9,15.1],[15.1,15.68],[15.68,16.4],[16.4,16.6],[16.6,17.0],[17.0,17.3],[17.3,17.65],[17.65,18.0],[19.0,19.5],[19.5,19.8],[19.8,20.2],[20.2,20.4],[20.4,20.9],[20.9,21.74],[21.74,21.9],[21.9,22.52],[22.7,23.1],[23.1,24.1],[24.1,24.83],[24.96,25.21],[25.21,25.6],[25.6,26.03],[26.03,26.58],[26.58,27.67],[27.67,28.36],[28.36,28.55],[28.55,28.85],[28.85,29.14],[29.14,29.3],[29.3,29.77],[29.77,30.4],[30.4,31.4],[31.4,31.8],[31.8,32.16],[32.16,32.4],[32.4,32.8],[32.8,33.3],[33.3,34.4],[34.4,34.6],[34.6,35.1],[35.1,35.5],[35.5,35.9],[35.9,36.7],[36.7,37.0],[37.0,37.2],[37.2,37.4],[38.44,38.84],[38.84,39.14],[39.14,39.34],[39.34,39.74],[39.74,40.04]],"female":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.9],[0.9,1.3],[1.3,1.8],[1.8,2.35],[2.35,3.3],[3.3,3.8],[3.8,4.4],[4.4,4.83],[4.83,5.48],[5.48,6.1],[6.1,6.6],[6.6,6.8],[6.8,7.1],[7.1,8.2],[8.2,8.5],[8.5,9.4],[9.4,9.8],[9.8,11.0],[11.0,11.4],[11.4,11.8],[11.8,12.48],[12.48,13.2],[13.25,13.5],[13.5,13.96],[13.96,14.3],[14.3,15.5],[15.5,16.0],[16.0,16.2],[16.2,16.4],[16.4,17.7],[17.7,17.9],[17.9,18.3],[18.3,18.6],[18.6,19.0],[19.0,19.4],[20.48,20.98],[20.98,21.28],[21.28,21.68],[21.68,21.88],[21.88,22.38],[22.38,22.75],[22.75,23.88],[23.88,24.6],[24.92,